/*  isis_ring.in  --  ISIS ring, ELEMEDGE placement, OPALX
    10 superperiods, circumference 163.363 m. 70 MeV kinetic proton pencil bunch
    (total energy 1008.272 MeV, as in the original deck), simple GAUSS
    distribution, no space charge. Turns are set by MAXSTEPS (ZSTOP far beyond
    the path): ~14900 steps per turn at DT = 1e-10 (beta = 0.366), so
    MAXSTEPS = 45000 is ~3 turns.

    Adapted from the legacy OPAL-cycl deck. Substitutions needed for OPALX:
    - DIST1 FROMFILE -> GAUSS pencil bunch with an emission source.
    - The 10 main dipoles (sp*_dip1) MULTIPOLET -> SBEND (same L, ELEMEDGE and
      ANGLE; 10 x 0.628319 rad = 2 pi). Reason: ELEMEDGE placement only turns
      the reference path at SBEND/RBEND, so MULTIPOLET dipoles would lay the
      ring out straight. The SBEND field (0.1758 T at 70 MeV) matches the
      original TP={-0.175827926} magnitude.
    - SCALING_MODEL removed from all MULTIPOLETs and the VARIABLE_RF_CAVITYs
      replaced by 1 m drifts (same names/positions): the referenced time
      dependence models (MagnetAmplitude, RfPhase*, ...) are not defined in
      this file and OPALX aborts on the name lookup. Coasting beam.
    - sp6_vbe (AC dipole) TP={0.001} -> {0.0}: without its AcDipoleScaler model
      a constant kick would accumulate every turn.
    - Quads etc. keep TP={0} from the original deck: no focusing defined.
    - Every DRIFT gets APERTURE = "ELLIPSE(0.3, 0.3)". Without one the default
      transverse bound is 1e6 m and drifts on the far side of the ring also
      claim the particle position (harmless for tracking, but it corrupts the
      element sets and cuts the element position file early).
*/

OPTION, PSDUMPFREQ   = 500;
OPTION, STATDUMPFREQ = 100;
OPTION, BOUNDPDESTROY = 10;
Option, VERSION = 10900;

Title, string="ISIS ring, ELEMEDGE placement, coasting 70 MeV protons";

REAL n_particles       = 1000;
REAL beam_bunch_charge = 1.6e-15;          // total bunch charge [C]

REAL Edes  = 0.07;                         // Kinetic energy [GeV]
REAL gamma = (Edes + PMASS) / PMASS;
REAL beta  = sqrt(1 - (1 / gamma^2));
REAL P0    = gamma * beta * PMASS;         // Reference momentum [GeV/c]

REAL bend_angle = 0.628319;                // 2 pi / 10 [rad]

value, {P0, gamma, beta};

sp0_dr1 : DRIFT, L=0.525, ELEMEDGE=0, APERTURE="ELLIPSE(0.3, 0.3)";
sp0_dr2a : DRIFT, L=0.2055, ELEMEDGE=0.525, APERTURE="ELLIPSE(0.3, 0.3)";
sp0_dr2b : DRIFT, L=1.4875, ELEMEDGE=0.7305, APERTURE="ELLIPSE(0.3, 0.3)";
sp0_dr3a : DRIFT, L=0.207, ELEMEDGE=2.218, APERTURE="ELLIPSE(0.3, 0.3)";
sp0_dr3b : DRIFT, L=0.6198996, ELEMEDGE=2.425, APERTURE="ELLIPSE(0.3, 0.3)";
sp0_qd : MULTIPOLET, L=0.7302008, ELEMEDGE=3.0448996, HAPERT=2, VAPERT=2, MAXFORDER=4, TP={0}, LFRINGE=0.07, RFRINGE=0.07, ANGLE=0;
sp0_dr4 : DRIFT, L=0.2031496, ELEMEDGE=3.7751004, APERTURE="ELLIPSE(0.3, 0.3)";
